    "done_when": "Measured 2026-09-29 against reckon.service at 2309c8b9: GET /_projects/index.json returns no response at all (connection closed, status 0) because one mounted project, imas-codex, holds a plan page the parser correctly refuses (docs/plans/migration-project-state.html: ValueError \"sections[''].id: record must be adjacent to its h2\", raised in reckon/_plan_html.py _read_section_records). In reckon/serve.py the rollup's project_entry (around line 672) catches only (OSError, ProjectStateError) around fleet_index.compute_project_row, so the ValueError escapes pool.map inside the ThreadPoolExecutor and the handler thread dies. the per-project route /_discover/imas-codex already turns the same refusal into a structured 500, so one malformed page in any mount currently empties the whole project list. Evidence: ~/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/page-load-20260929/report.md section 3.\n\n(1) Make the rollup isolate a project's plan-parse refusal: the other projects' rows are served, and the failing project's row carries a structured error naming the refused file and the refusal text. Catch the parser's refusal specifically: find where _plan_html raises and whether a named exception type exists or should be introduced; do not widen the handler to a bare Exception, and do not change _plan_html's decision to refuse the page.\n(2) tests/test_rollup_isolates_a_project.py, in tmp_path (the pytest fixture) with every mount and state directory environment-resolved to tmp_path: three synthesised mounts, one holding a plan page with the same malformation (a section record carrying id= and no data-id, no adjacent h2), drive the /_projects/index.json handler and assert 200, both good rows intact, and the bad project's row carrying the error with the file name. Negative control: restore today's except clause; the request must fail. Assert the real ~/.config/reckon is untouched afterwards.\n(3) The existing serve and page-load tests add no failures against the base, by id, with pytest basetemp outside any git repository: tests/test_fleet_index.py, tests/test_discovery_reads_each_file_once.py and tests/test_shell_project_list_is_immediate.py. Record baseline_suite and after_suite as JSON objects with log_path and failure_ids.\nLogs under the run directory, each headed with revision, tree and literal command, ending with an EXIT= line and the failing test ids. The gate command names the absolute .venv python. Commit in this worktree. Do not restart reckon.service; the coordinator re-takes the warm gate after the merge.",
